ple) were excluded for missing skin tone ratings due to unavailable photos", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["exclusions", "skin tone"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 52, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[81, 81]], "assertion": "14,598 dyads with medium skin tone were excluded to create a clear light-vs-dark comparison", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["exclusions", "skin tone"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 53, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[82, 86]], "assertion": "dyads missing covariates were excluded: position (7,700), height (46), weight (686), implicit/explicit bias scores (122)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["exclusions", "covariates"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 54, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[87, 87]], "assertion": "the total complete-case sample is 101,718 dyads, 69.7% of the original 146,028", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["analysis sample"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 55, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[88, 88]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 56, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[89, 89]], "note": "Transformations subheading"}, {"id": 57, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[90, 90]], "assertion": "skin tone was computed as the average of two independent raters' assessments, normalized to a 0-1 scale", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["skin tone"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 58, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[91, 91]], "assertion": "a log1p transform was applied to the games variable to handle right skew", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["games"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 59, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[92, 92]], "assertion": "height and weight were standardized to z-scores", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["height", "weight"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 60, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[93, 93]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 61, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[94, 94]], "note": "SE/Weighting/Fixed Effects subheading"}, {"id": 62, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[95, 95]], "assertion": "standard errors were clustered by player across 1,242 clusters", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["standard errors"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 63, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[96, 96]], "assertion": "player or referee fixed effects were not used, since skin tone would be collinear with player fixed effects", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["fixed effects"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 64, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[97, 97]], "assertion": "the analysis was unweighted, with each dyad weighted equally", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["weighting"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 65, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[98, 100]], "note": "separator"}, {"id": 66, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[101, 102]], "note": "Conclusion heading"}, {"id": 67, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[103, 103]], "assertion": "the hypothesis of referee red-card bias against dark-skinned players is not supported by the analysis", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 68, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[104, 104]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 69, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[105, 106]], "note": "Reasons subheading"}, {"id": 70, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[107, 107]], "note": "reason 1 label"}, {"id": 71, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[108, 108]], "assertion": "the primary estimand's p-value (0.256) is well above the α=0.05 threshold", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["p-value", "risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 72, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[109, 109]], "assertion": "the secondary estimand's p-value (0.140) is 