fect size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 83, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[120, 120]], "assertion": "the practical/clinical significance of the small effect size is questionable", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect size"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 84, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[121, 121]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 85, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[122, 122]], "note": "reason 4 label"}, {"id": 86, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[123, 127]], "assertion": "stratified league estimates vary widely: Germany +0.58pp, England +0.26pp, Spain -0.48pp, France -0.61pp", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["league", "stratified analysis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 87, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[128, 128]], "assertion": "the heterogeneity suggests the aggregate effect may not represent a consistent underlying phenomenon", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect heterogeneity"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 88, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[129, 129]], "assertion": "the positive aggregate effect may be driven primarily by Germany and England, while France and Spain show the opposite pattern", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["league", "aggregate effect"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 89, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[130, 130]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 90, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[131, 131]], "note": "reason 5 label"}, {"id": 91, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[132, 132]], "assertion": "the unadjusted risk difference (0.097pp) is slightly smaller than the adjusted estimate", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 92, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[133, 133]], "assertion": "clustering by referee instead of player gives a similar point estimate but a different SE and p